  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Open Ledger",
    "overview": "TRT Ledger is a price guide that shows its working. The system is the category standard for consumer health comparison, executed at full craft: large rounded panels, pill controls, one confident ink color, and condensed heavy numerals that make a first-year total the loudest thing on any surface it appears on. Every visual decision serves one act: reading a sourced number, seeing how sure the site is of it, and acting on it.\n\nThe default first visit is **dark**: a deep blue-black ground with periwinkle actions. A stored choice from the header sun/moon switch can flip the site to the light world of soft blue-gray grounds and navy ink; both themes are full peers built from the same custom properties, and every generated state, city and partner page applies the same pre-paint theme script. Density is moderate: comparison cards carry a lot of facts, so the system spends its contrast on totals and status, and keeps everything else quiet in muted ink.\n\nImagery is limited to one authored stroke-icon set and the logo mark. There are no photographs, stock people, or illustrations.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark by default; light is a stored opt-in with identical structure.",
      "Archivo variable throughout: condensed extra-bold for display and figures, regular width for UI.",
      "Tabular figures on every price.",
      "Pills for every control and status tag; large-radius panels for every container.",
      "Three status colors with fixed meanings: green confirmed/savings, amber check, red errors.",
      "One authored motion moment; everything else is a short state transition."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three Meanings Rule",
        "body": "Green means confirmed for your state or money saved; amber means check this; red means something is wrong with input. No status color is ever decoration. The build currently also tints the \"not included\" cross in clinic inclusion lists red; that use is under review and is not a pattern to extend.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Confirmed-Only Green Rule",
        "body": "\"Lowest first-year cost\" and its green treatment go only to a clinic confirmed to serve the visitor's state. A clinic that does not publish its states gets amber \"Check state\", never green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Action Color Rule",
        "body": "Periwinkle (dark) or navy (light) is the only action fill. Secondary actions are surface-colored pills with a hairline, not a second accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Width Axis Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy is carried by width and weight together: display and figures sit between wdth 72 and 85 at 800–850; UI text stays at wdth 100. Never set body copy condensed, and never set a total at regular width.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Price Rule",
        "body": "Every price, count, distance and stat uses tabular figures so columns of totals align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase labels, tracked-out eyebrows or kickers above headings. A heading starts the section.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Lift Rule",
        "body": "Shadows are ambient and the same at rest everywhere; there is no hover lift on cards. State is shown by color and border, not by elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** treat dark as the default first visit and design every new surface in both themes from the shared custom properties.",
      "**Do** make the first-year total the largest, most condensed text on any card (850, wdth 75, tabular).",
      "**Do** pair every price with its \"Checked [date]\" and a Source link with the outbound icon.",
      "**Do** use amber \"Check state\" for any clinic that does not publish its states, and reserve \"Lowest first-year cost\" and its green for a clinic confirmed for the visitor's state.",
      "**Do** keep every control a pill at 44px or taller on phones.",
      "**Do** draw any new icon to the existing 24px, 2px round-cap stroke."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a second accent color or use green, amber or red decoratively.",
      "**Don't** use photographs, stock people, clinic imagery or illustrations.",
      "**Don't** add eyebrows, kickers or uppercase tracked labels above headings.",
      "**Don't** use hard offset shadows or hover lifts on cards.",
      "**Don't** add motion beyond the overpaying result's settle-in; state changes are 0.15s color transitions.",
      "**Don't** use emoji or text glyphs as icons."
    ]
  }
}
